  "descriptionKey": "- Available seat-kilometres measure how much passenger-carrying capacity airlines offered.\n- One available seat-kilometre equals one seat flown one kilometre, whether it was filled or empty.\n- A flight with 200 seats flying 1,000 kilometres generates 200,000 available seat-kilometres.\n- This metric combines seat numbers and distances flown, so it is more informative than flight counts alone.\n- It measures capacity offered, not how many passengers actually traveled.",
